NAME
        str2val - Convert a string format variable back to a variable.

SYNOPSYS
        mixed str2val(string str)

DESCRIPTION
	The main use of this function is to process a variable that has
	been converted into a string format via the efun 'val2str'.

	Use of this function directly is discouraged.  You should be
	using the save/restore_map, save/restore_object functions for
	saving and retrieving data.

        Deserialization accepts at most 8 MiB of input, 131072 values total,
        and 64 value levels (including the outermost value). Object names
        must fit in 1023 bytes. Malformed or over-budget input returns 0.
        The same value limits apply when restoring objects and mappings.

SEE ALSO
	val2str, save_object, save_map, restore_object, restore_map

